            "review_title": "Review at Banh Mi Hanoi",
            "review_text": "bigyam77\nHong Kong, China94 contributions\n0\nGreat fillings, Shame about the bun!\nMar 2014 • Solo\nI had great hopes for Banh Mi Hanoi, as even my driver perked up when I told him I wanted to go there. \n\nThe baguette is on the large side, and there is a generous portion of fillings. I had the traditional, with pate, ham, sliced porky goodness, pickly veggies and of course coriander.\n\nThe filling is good, and due to the generous portion, better than most. I would have liked more acidity in the pickles, but that's very subjective. Overall, good fillings.\n\nBUT: what about the baguette? It is not the lightest nor crispiest out there. This is a big strike against any Banh Mi. Put it this way...when biting all the way through the Banh Mi in one bite, you can feel your jaws strain. A good Banh Mi can a) be compressed (by lightly smashing the sandwich before eating, while it's still in the paper wrapper) and then b) easily bitten through. This one was a workout for the jaws.\n\nNot sure if it would have been different during different times of day, or perhaps they can, like some others do, either keep it over heat for crisping or have a toasteroven handy to crisp it up. As it was, today at least, it was too chewy/tough for this aficionado.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 20, 2014",
