            "review_title": "Review at Banh Mi Hanoi",
            "review_text": "Journeyman1971\nSingapore, Singapore59 contributions\n0\nDelivered on what it promised\nJul 2013 • Family\nWe asked for a place that had the best banh mi hands down in Ho Chi Minh and were directed to this place. Its a bit of a dive and the people working there don't seem to speak much English but fortunately we had a driver that could help translate. My wife didn't care for it and even though I got a fairly plain sandwich (I think there were still some translation issues) with just a baguette and shredded chicken filling, for such a no-frills, no-sides and no-sauce sandwich it was delicious. The baguette was nice and fresh and the chicken filling had a very tasty sweet and savory flavor. I'd definitely return to see if my sandwich was in line with how the locals like it.\nRead more\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 30, 2013",
